old #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]monitor_custom_statuses.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/monitor_custom_statuses.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-qv[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-qv/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor status contract module[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]contract[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]contract: add the shared sase.monitor_status module that owns the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default labels, the 20-character clamp, pair normalization, the 12-color[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]accent palette, and the state-aware style rule; retire the scattered [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]MONITORING/MONITORED literals onto it.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Required start and stop status flags[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: make -s/--start-status and -S/--stop-status required on sase [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor start, clamp over-length labels with a warning, make the two [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fields required on StartMonitorRequest, and render the effective label [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]in sase monitor list, show, markdown, and JSON.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Status pair plumbing and terminality[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]model[dim] · [dim][/dim]after contract[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]model: carry monitor_stop_status alongside monitor_start_status through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the scan-wire and filesystem loaders, the TUI Agent row, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]RunningAgentInfo, the integrations entry, and the mobile summary; fix [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]settled monitors with custom stop labels being treated as non-terminal.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Agents tab and agent list coloring[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]agents_tab[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]agents_tab: color the monitor status token by its pair accent in the ACE[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent list, add the outcome glyphs that replace the retired success [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]green, add a Status field to the prompt panel MONITOR section, and color[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase agent list STATUS badge.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Agent family container status[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]family[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]family: mirror a monitor's custom status onto its agent family container[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]row for plain families as well as plan roots, and copy the status pair [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so the mirrored row renders in the same accent as the monitor itself.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Procs tab monitor status chip[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]procs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after model[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]procs: resolve each monitor proc row's status pair from the loaded agent[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rows and render the effective label as an accent-colored chip in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Admin Center Procs tab row labels and output header.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Guidance, skill, and docs[/bold #D7AFFF]                                     [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]guidance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli, agents_tab[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]guidance: teach TESTING/TESTED in the build-and-run memory note, make [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the sase_monitor skill and monitors/ACE/CLI docs state that both flags [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]are required, and regenerate the derived instruction files.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-qv","llm_provider":"grok","model":"grok-4.6","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-qv.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-8bcd3cf1c97a361acb91a0ba53afd50c","started_at":"2026-08-19T13:15:50.754097+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"ea0247de0bb75c434a038e2280eb67f98971bb62ffadfc1f0168f061a0eb21be","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.land--plan/chat.md","size_bytes":5781},"commits":{"digest":"fea777fef155f638f86670449933fe697745dcdaa2a2b2eff79d29871a9831e7","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.land--plan/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.land--plan/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"cbeb784b5524408e9bda5c36a21824a811def11fa5b70de92581355f5d94b48a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.land--plan/meta.json","size_bytes":692},"prompt":{"digest":"9dc8881a2abcd67579fd4326d39c6ec8fa916b008b9221b60aaf3c6a1de1fb07","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv.land--plan/prompt.md","size_bytes":295},"prompt_steps":{"digest":"6041d72403805e117bbaaae21037988cd959379e760133190eccb8c4dacdbe68","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-qv